+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# Full-layer VERIFY (q_len 8, causal inside the block) at 1 < batch <= 64 (tp8, page 1): rewrite stage 1 of the
+# warp-specialized wgmma line (full-verify-wgmma-ws-s1-producer-split), module muse_full_verify_wgmma_ws_v1, kernel
+# symbols wsv1_*, python names _ws_* / _wsv_* (none shared with the sibling split-ring-2cta build). Built on stage 5's
+# proven math (full-verify-wgmma-s5-qfrag-reload, 19 bisect cases and two-state replays passed): SW128 K/V ring filled by
+# 16-byte cp.async.cg, stream-K over TILE-token tiles, fp8 QK wgmma m64nTILEk32 with the per-tile Q A-fragment reload from
+# shared memory, FA3 Max_offset-8 FP8 P, per-warpgroup V^T transpose, in-kernel ticket combine + norm-gate epilogue.
+# Only the pipeline changes:
+#  variant 0 "ws64"  : 384 threads, 1 CTA/SM. WG0 = producer (setmaxnreg.dec 56): its 128 threads issue every K/V tile
+#                      (8 cp.async per thread per 64-token tile; page indices prefetched 4 tiles ahead in registers)
+#                      and arrive (cp.async.mbarrier.arrive.noinc) on FULL[st]; it waits EMPTY[st] (256 consumer
+#                      arrivals) only to refill stage st. WG1/WG2 = consumers (setmaxnreg.inc 224), kv head 0/1, never
+#                      load. 8-stage ring of 16 KB. Two S accumulator sets: S(n+1) is issued before softmax(n), PV(n-1)
+#                      is issued before S(n+1) and awaited with wgmma.wait_group 1, so tensor-core work overlaps softmax.
+#  variant 1 "ws128" : the same with TILE = 128 (m64n128k32 S, 4 PV k-steps), 5 stages of 32 KB (160 KB ring), ONE S
+#                      accumulator set (two sets of 64 registers would not fit 224 with the softmax temporaries): FA3
+#                      order, PV(n-1) overlaps softmax(n).
+#  variant 2 "c2"    : s5's layout (2 CTAs/SM, 256 threads, every thread issues cp.async) with the ring split per
+#                      warpgroup (one ring of 8 KB stages per kv head, per-warpgroup FULL/EMPTY barriers of 128 arrivals,
+#                      no CTA-wide rendezvous), single S set, FA3 order (PV(n-1) overlaps softmax(n)). 5 stages.
+#  variant 3         : ws64 with the PHASE DIAG (clock64 stamps per phase, CTA 0), prepare only, never timed or routed.
+# Every variant also takes a runtime GO flag (gather-only roofline DIAG): same ring and producer, consumers just wait
+# FULL and arrive EMPTY, no math, no output.
+# All wgmma / mbarrier / setmaxnreg code sits under __CUDA_ARCH_FEAT_SM90_ALL; any other image only sets the device error
+# flag (bit 1), which the self-check reads. Every mbarrier wait is bounded (clock64 -> error bit 2 + CTA abort flag).
+# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
